MITOSIS is a personal research project. It is not published under an
open-source licence, and no permission is granted to use, copy, modify,
distribute, or create derivative works from it.

This file exists to state that plainly rather than leave it to be inferred.
A repository with no LICENSE file is already all-rights-reserved by default,
but a reader has no way to tell that from an oversight — and "the author
forgot" and "the author decided" call for different behaviour from anyone who
finds it.

If this is ever published, replacing this file with an open-source licence is
a one-commit change. Doing so in the other direction is not: terms cannot be
retracted from versions someone already has, so the permissive choice is the
one that has to wait until it is meant.
